# This file is a WHITELIST, as the project rules require.
# Everything is ignored by default. Only the source file types listed
# below are tracked. Game assets, extracted game files, decompiled code,
# logs and build output are never tracked, because they never match.
# Add a new "!" line here only for a new kind of source file.

# 1. Ignore everything.
*

# 2. Let git look inside folders (this alone tracks no files).
!*/

# 3. Track only these source and project files.
!.gitignore
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!*.rs
!*.md
# Our own shaders (GPU programs).
!crates/**/*.wgsl
!crates/**/*.wesl
# Game settings files that mods can edit (our own, never the game's).
!data/**/*.toml
# Automatic checks on GitHub (our own workflow files).
!.github/workflows/*.yml

# 4. Never look inside these folders, even if a file in them matches above.
# Rust build output.
target/
# Places for game data extracted at runtime. Keep game files here.
extracted/
game-data/
